(D9 — Discrepancy 9 repro: LANGUAGE.md:3046-3047 calls `respectively`
 "reserved as a possible future marker for a zip mode; it is not parsed
 today". It is genuinely not parsed — this sentence is a compile error —
 but it is NOT reserved as an identifier: `a number called respectively is
 4.` compiles and prints 4 (see LST2-71.vox). A program that uses the name
 today would break when the zip marker lands.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D9.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Unknown function: respectively
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
To pair of a number called left and a number called right.
  print "{left}-{right}".

'pair' of each x from [1, 2] and each y from [10, 20] respectively.
